I ran into this on v1.2.11 with Kimi K2.5 and K2 Thinking on Bedrock. PR #14586 fixes the empty-string content case, but there's a second path that still produces empty content after that fix.

The interleaved reasoning filter at `transform.ts:136-169` runs *after* the empty content guard at lines 52-72. When a model has `interleaved: { field: "reasoning_content" }`, it strips reasoning parts from `content` and moves them to `providerOptions`. If an assistant message has only reasoning parts (no text or tool-call), `filteredContent` becomes `[]`. The empty content guard already ran at that point, so nothing catches this.

I applied PR #14586's change locally and confirmed the bug still reproduces:

```typescript
const msgs = [
  { role: "user", content: "hello" },
  {
    role: "assistant",
    content: [
      { type: "reasoning", text: "Let me think about this..." },
    ],
  },
  { role: "user", content: "go on" },
] as any[]

const result = ProviderTransform.message(msgs, kimiK2_5BedrockModel, {})
// result[1].content === []  still empty even with #14586 applied
```

The empty content guard at line 62 keeps these parts because their text is not empty. They have real content. Then the interleaved filter at line 144 strips them anyway. A post-filter check in the interleaved block, or moving the empty content guard to run after all transforms, would catch this.

Also, once this hits, switching to Claude Opus in the same session doesn't help. The empty message is stuck in the history and breaks every model until you start a new session.
